{"title":"2011 CSMC Problems/Part B Problem 1 Part A","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_CSMC_Problems/Part_B_Problem_1\" title=\"2011 CSMC Problems/Part B Problem 1\">Problem 1</a></span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_CSMC_Problems/Part_B_Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=T-1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The parabola with equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/b/52b54caabec11d7639d2439b8b545ff741170f0e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = 25 - x^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"94\" height=\"20\" /> intersects the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />-axis at points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, as shown.\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2011_CSMC_Problems/Part_B_Problem_1_Part_A&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_CSMC_Problems/Part_B_Problem_1_Part_A&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Determine the length of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_CSMC_Problems/Part_B_Problem_1_Part_A&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> are the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />-intercepts of the parabola, so for points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/6/d86391274aef65dfe355c32b7667500b54c9a986.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 = 25 - x^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"93\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/e/34e52d07ac8fae3a35c6d7a57070b2efcd0b30ff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-x^{2} = 0 - 25 = -25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"164\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/5/0b5026c996c0feb67a06f18e9064c9b6594ccbe5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^{2} = \\frac{-25}{-1} = 25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"123\" height=\"40\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/f/29fa31bf156fcd79f39afeb9b6187bbb209efa2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = \\pm \\sqrt{25} = \\pm 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"131\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p>Alternatively, we could have factored <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/e/2de1042d3aa9fb9c2cec9e0295935d261c32d87e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$25 - x^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"60\" height=\"18\" /> into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/4/e746695251cc70fa77a957a2bd4df41e5497595a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(5 - x)(5 + x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"114\" height=\"20\" /> and find that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/1/e2198bae8cf88ca13ff4a11a0ac2f94974923867.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5 - x = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"77\" height=\"15\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/d/84d38f832e7345e50d4081af670d7028d449e912.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5 + x = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"77\" height=\"15\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/3/c43970aa97091f384854d477a1e1e07356887266.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/f/6ef1c4328c03cd2021b41b653218a5778379397b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = -5$\" width=\"57\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p><p>This means that point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> is at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/c/54c6d8abfb452e39157f93c7dc806649a81e9bb6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(-5, 0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"53\" height=\"18\" /> and point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> is at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/5/b25d38afb38cb21e729f74fc5a880d03d5368e3c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(5, 0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />. The length of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> is then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/9/ed9ef39fbee57c92203a6faeda109d1223a0f093.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5 - (-5) = \\boxed{10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"124\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018054813\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.016 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.024 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 96/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1000/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 5/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 4600/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   13.250      1 2011_CSMC_Problems/Part_B_Problem_1\n100.00%   13.250      1 -total\n 39.34%    5.212      1 Template:Image_needed\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:37293:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018054813 and revision id 287949. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}